{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-16_15-11-32-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run; cat draft/update36.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"Closed the empty-command question's disposition and recorded a synthesis Fact for the recovery-value handling family, so the four defects this run asserts share one navigable statement with their distinct responsibilities and receipts. No measurement changed.\",\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@fact-recovery-value-handling-family\",\n      \"kind\": \"fact\",\n      \"statement\": \"In the captured EPaxos package the value a recovery adopts is not protected by the quorum that holds it: four distinct mechanisms of the same recovery path each let a recovering replica end up proposing, and then deciding, a value other than the one its prepare replies carry. (a) startRecoveryForInstance fabricates a value ballot for its own empty state, so the adoption loop skips genuine replies (epaxos/epaxos.go:1145-1165, 1239-1246). (b) A reply whose value ballot is at most the fabricated one is ignored even when it reports the highest accepted value, so a NOOP replaces an accepted value, including one another live replica has already committed. (c) A reply that reports the instance COMMITTED is discarded once its status reaches lb.status, because the pre-accept guard then rejects the remaining replies, so the first recovery attempt stalls until the retry (epaxos/epaxos.go:870-881, 1255-1313). (d) A reply that carries no command decodes as a non-nil empty slice, which the sub-case 5/6 fallback passes to startPhase1 instead of state.NOOP() (epaxos/defs.go:228-235, epaxos/epaxos.go:1307-1311), and which command is adopted is fixed by the replies present when the slow-quorum trigger fires, so arrival order alone can decide whether the owner's command survives. Recovering replicas that already hold the value are not affected by (a)-(b), and the client re-offer protects the single-NOOP case but not the empty-slice case.\",\n      \"conditions\": \"N=5, F=2 configuration of the captured snapshot with Thrifty on and IsLeader false at the recovering replica; the instance owner fails inside its accept window and the recovering replica holds the instance without its command, or (for the arrival-order variant) recovers its own instance while replies at the same value ballot differ.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-decl-recovery\",\n        \"s-recovery-init\",\n        \"s-prepare-reply-adopt\",\n        \"s-subcase-dispatch\",\n        \"s-preaccept-reply\",\n        \"s-prepare-reply-unmarshal\",\n        \"s-commit-repropose\",\n        \"s-decl-prepare-reply\"\n      ],\n      \"knowledge\": [\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"2b0dd5bd3ea84bdeba83de7f4c680c00-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 3,\n          \"assertion\": \"empty slice adopted and passed through with the trigger timing deciding the command\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"cbbf11dd38d843f1b6acf52fd5b6e82e-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 3,\n          \"assertion\": \"COMMITTED status adopted then later replies discarded\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"entry_id\": \"ed76b573b9fe4bde9565d4b4678cda85-knowledge-0\",\n          \"revision\": 2,\n          \"assertion\": \"a recovery lacking the command can decide a different value than a live replica's committed value\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"executions\": {\n        \"143e14592eea4c42b3c81044e3860348\": [\n          7,\n          8,\n          9,\n          11,\n          14,\n          16,\n          17,\n          19,\n          20,\n          21,\n          22,\n          23\n        ],\n        \"d80cbfd9f9a547639811aeacb19c0a30\": [\n          6,\n          10,\n          11,\n          16,\n          19,\n          21,\n          24,\n          25,\n          26,\n          27\n        ],\n        \"e89ecb076e8d4a78b174f848562ed77f\": [\n          6,\n          13,\n          20\n        ],\n        \"098ab4425325464192aa558be557f0ce\": [\n          3,\n          4\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"investigations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"0757162a4aa64ef4a58a90002641eb27-question-0\",\n      \"disposition\": \"explained\",\n      \"hypothesis\": \"The adoption loop takes any reply whose VBallot is at least the running candidate ballot and copies its command into the candidate, so a reply at the same value ballot that carries no command can replace the command the owner itself contributed; because the dispatch fires when the appended replies reach the slow quorum, which reply is adopted last depends on arrival order, and with two empty replies against one command-carrying reply two of the three exercised orders lose the command while the third keeps it.\",\n      \"discriminator\": \"Whether the remaining three permutations of the three peer replies behave as the trigger position predicts, and whether a scenario with more command-carrying replies than empty ones flips the outcome.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
